    description: "**Measured 2026-08-01 on dev 54a5f34bcc** (the item's own subcommand, the\nright instrument — NOT the hg.4k/16k/64k budget views, which are the sketch\nside and mismeasured this item once before, corrected 2026-07-16).\n\n**Repro** (input maps = the 2026-07-17 bakeoff artifacts, deep-20260717-200119):\n\n    hypergumbo compact --input <repo>/hg.json --max-symbols N --out cN.json\n    for N in 10 25 50 100; assert nodes(c10) <= nodes(c25) <= nodes(c50) <= nodes(c100)\n\n**Result: containment VIOLATED on 6 of 8 repos; express and pretix clean.**\n\n    caddy            VIOLATED 50->100  (drops Dispenser.Val, Dispenser.Next, fmt.Errorf +2)\n    apollo-server    VIOLATED 50->100  (drops jest globals describe/expect/it)\n    SwiftyJSON       VIOLATED 10->25   (drops JSON.encode, JSON.exists, ComparableTests)\n    zoxide           VIOLATED 25->50 AND 50->100 (drops Query.query_interactive/_list/_first)\n    spring-petclinic VIOLATED 25->50 AND 50->100 (drops PetValidator.validate ...)\n    sherpa-csharp    VIOLATED at every step (10->25, 25->50, 50->100)\n    express          OK\n    pretix           OK\n\nDeterministic: two identical caddy --max-symbols 100 runs produce identical\nnode sets; the c50-minus-c100 difference is stable at 5 nodes. So this is a\nselection-logic property, not tie-break nondeterminism.\n\n**Consistency with the record:** the 2026-07-16 correction verified\n--max-symbols monotonic on pretix — pretix IS clean here too. The\nverification was real but pretix-only; six other repos violate. Note the\ndropped nodes at larger budgets include both real methods AND\nexternal_symbols, and several sweeps did not fill their budget (SwiftyJSON\nsizes 10/12/25/50 for budgets 10/25/50/100) — the --coverage 0.8 default\ninteracting with selection is a plausible mechanism surface, unverified.\n\n**Provenance:** found while validating the awaits_bakeoff_validation queue;\nthe 8 reflect assessments' moved=6 plurality for the parent measured the\nbudget-view artifacts, which do NOT exercise this subcommand. Sweep script\nand outputs preserved in the session scratchpad (compact_sweep.py)."  # e339
